[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Basic Verification using verify() in Mockito"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Verification in Mockito is used to check whether certain methods have been called with specific arguments on your mock objects. This tutorial demonstrates how to use the verify() method effectively in your unit tests."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Before using Mockito's verify() method, ensure you have included the Mockito dependency in your project and statically imported the Mockito methods to keep your test code clean."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"import static org.mockito.Mockito.*;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.mockito.Mockito;"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding verify()"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"By default, verify() checks that a method was called exactly once. If the method was never called, or called a different number of times, the test will fail with a WantedButNotInvoked or NeverWanted exception."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Code Example: Basic Method Invocation"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Consider a scenario where a service relies on an external UserRepository to delete a user by ID. We want to verify that the delete method was triggered."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"@Test
public void testUserDeletion() {
    // 1. Create mock
    UserRepository mockRepository = mock(UserRepository.class);

    // 2. Execute business logic
    UserService userService = new UserService(mockRepository);
    userService.removeUser(42L);

    // 3. Verify interaction
    verify(mockRepository).delete(42L);
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Key Takeaways"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"verify(mockObject) acts on a mock instance to check subsequent method calls."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Exact matching of arguments is enforced by default (e.g., verifying delete(42L) will fail if delete(43L) was called)."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Verification ensures behavioral correctness without relying solely on return values."}]
